{"agent":"buglane28","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new predicate suppresses the `expired_lease` finding for every terminal item, not only for terminal items that are actually clean-and-fully-merged as the bug motivates. Given an item that is terminal (e.g. completed or cancelled) but whose lapsed lease still has/points to a worktree containing unmerged changes, `_expired_lease` returns `False` solely because `it.terminal` is true, so `scan` skips the entire expired-lease branch. That branch contains the logic that prefers whichever source names a tree and surfaces real salvageable work; before this change, the same input would enter the branch and report an expired-lease/salvage finding. The result is a false negative for real unmerged work, while the stated fix was only meant to stop clean merged done items from being labelled `[expired_lease]`.","digest":"523fec17148261f6","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/leases/recovery.py:_expired_lease","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/leases/recovery.py:_expired_lease"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":3128,"diff_sha":"b5d9fbfb94d586f8d066155e1d818aceb31f69fd1626f5fe95e38e1e21054863","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-Ba73b94a6ad","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":204.7,"family":"alibaba","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"6d597189d84692ee","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-Ba73b94a6ad.rubber_duck.[REDACTED:name].20261113T222150Z-d0905f4d.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"fe29d7309e56b5fd00edfb86ad57a8c3396fc597","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/services/leases/recovery.py":"100644 38823ff17c462cf03578d48aaa292ec3a1b023cd","tests/test_recover_merged_item.